g from T11): T11 \u2192 T1 \u2192 W1 \u2192 B8 \u2192 T7 \u2192 C \u2192 B5 \u2192 T11. Size 7, same set as slots 3/4: {T1, W1, B8, T7, C, B5, T11}.\nSo:\nP0's wheel: {T11, T1, W1, B8, T7, C, B5} \u2014 top glyphs: T11, T1, T7.\nP1's wheel: {plus, M1, X2, X3, X4, X5, T5} \u2014 top: T5.\nP2's wheel: {B7, T5, T11, T1, W1, X1, T7} \u2014 top: T5, T11, T1, T7.\nP3's wheel: {B8, T7, C, B5, T11, T1, W1} \u2014 top: T7, T11, T1.\nP4's wheel: {T1, W1, B8, T7, C, B5, T11} \u2014 top: T1, T7, T11.\nCurrently P0 = T11 (after 7 UPs, back to T11).\nCurrent P row: [T11, X3, B7, B8, T11].\nNow, the \"all top glyphs\" test: set P1\u2192T5 (from X3: 3 UPs), P2\u2192T5 (from B7: 1 UP), P3\u2192T11 (from B8: 4 UPs), P4=T11 \u2713, P0=T11 \u2713.\nThen check whether the level is complete. If not complete, the goal is something more specific, and we'll need to try target assignments.\nActually, before that, let me think about which specific assignment is most likely. If the goal is \"P row = some fixed target row,\" the targets must be within each wheel:\nP0 \u2208 {T1,T7,T11}, P1 = T5, P2 \u2208 {T1,T5,T7,T11}, P3 \u2208 {T1,T7,T11}, P4 \u2208 {T1,T7,T11}.\nA plausible target row: [T1, T5, T7, T11, ?] or [T11, T5, T7, T11, T1], etc.\nTop grid positions: T1=(0,1), T5=(1,1), T7=(1,3), T11=(2,3).\nHmm, what if the target is [T1, T5, T7, T11, T1]? Or the 5th slot is a duplicate of the 1st?\nOr maybe the target row is the top row 1 [T4,T5,T6,T7] extended with something: P1=T5 \u2713 (matches top(1,1)!), P2=T7? (top(1,2)=T6, no)...\nIf the target is [?, T5, T6, T7, ?] \u2014 P2 can't do T6. No.\nIf the target is [T1, T5, T7, T11, T1]: a zigzag path (0,1)\u2192(1,1)\u2192(1,3)\u2192(2,3)\u2192(2,1)?\nIf the target is [T7, T5, T1, T11, T1]?\nHonestly, the \"all top glyphs\" test is the best next probe: if the win condition is \"all P glyphs are within the palette,\" it'll complete. Let's run it:\n- Slot 1: 3 UPs (X3\u2192X4\u2192X5\u2192T5).\n- Slot 2: 1 UP (B7\u2192T5).\n- Slot 3: 4 UPs (B8\u2192T7\u2192C\u2192B5\u2192T11).\nSequence from slot 0: RIGHT (slot 1), UP\u00d73, RIGHT (slot 2), UP, RIGHT (slot 3), UP\u00d74.\nAfter that, check last_action_result for level completion.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": true}, {"label": "ASSISTANT", "content": "Slot 0's wheel = {T11,T1,W1,B8,T7,C,B5}. Now testing the \"all top-grid glyphs\" hypothesis: set P1\u2192T5, P2\u2192T5, P3\u2192T11 (P0, P4 already T11).", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\naction(['RIGHT'])   # slot 1\naction(['UP']*3)    # X3->X4->X5->T5\naction(['RIGHT'])   # slot 2\naction(['UP'])      # B7->T5\naction(['RIGHT'])   # slot 3\naction(['UP']*4)    # B8->T7->C->B5->T11\nprint(\"result:\", {k:last_action_result.get(k) for k in ('board_changed','done','level_completed','game_over','run_complete','reward')})\nfr = current_frame.ascii.split('\\n')\ncols = [(15,19),(22,26),(29,33),(36,40),(43,47)]\nfor i,(c1,c2) in enumerate(cols):\n    print(\"P\",i, ' '.join(''.join('#' if fr[r][c]=='B' else '.' for c in range(c1,c2+1)) for r in range(52,57)))\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL RESULT: python", "content": "result: {'board_changed': True, 'done': False, 'level_completed': False, 'game_over': False, 'run_complete': False, 'reward': 0.0}\nP 0 ..#.. ##### #.#.# ##### ..#..\nP 1 ##### #..#. #..#. ####. #....\nP 2 #.... ####. #..#. #..#. #####\nP 3 ..#.. ##### #.#.# ##### ..#..\nP 4 ..#.. ##### #.#.# ##### ..#..", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}], "hasExactModelContext": false, "requestIndexWithinTurn": null, "messageCount": 0}, "context": {"sections": [{"label": "USER PROMPT", "content": "The code executed 8 actions in the previous sequence.\nExecuted actions: LEFT, UP, UP, UP, UP, UP, UP, UP.\nYou are still on the same level.\nCurrent state: step 66, level 1.\nValid actions right now: UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT.\nEnd of carried world mo